Subject: [PATCH] WebRTC: offer BUNDLE for the default balanced policy

GStreamer 1.24 cannot implement balanced, but leaving its default NONE
omits a=group:BUNDLE and is incompatible with BUNDLE-only SFUs.
Use max-compat as the fallback: it offers BUNDLE while retaining separate
transport fallback. Preserve explicitly selected policies.

--- a/Source/WebCore/Modules/mediastream/gstreamer/GStreamerMediaEndpoint.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebCore/Modules/mediastream/gstreamer/GStreamerMediaEndpoint.cpp
@@ -378,12 +378,11 @@

 bool GStreamerMediaEndpoint::setConfiguration(MediaEndpointConfiguration& configuration)
 {
-    // Balanced bundle policy is currently not supported in webrtcbin and an error is emitted, so
-    // explicitely configure it only for the other cases.
-    if (configuration.bundlePolicy != RTCBundlePolicy::Balanced) {
-        auto bundlePolicy = bundlePolicyFromConfiguration(configuration);
-        g_object_set(m_webrtcBin.get(), "bundle-policy", bundlePolicy, nullptr);
-    }
+    // webrtcbin 1.24 does not implement balanced. max-compat still offers BUNDLE
+    // and retains separate transports when the remote endpoint cannot bundle.
+    auto bundlePolicy = configuration.bundlePolicy == RTCBundlePolicy::Balanced
+        ? GST_WEBRTC_BUNDLE_POLICY_MAX_COMPAT : bundlePolicyFromConfiguration(configuration);
+    g_object_set(m_webrtcBin.get(), "bundle-policy", bundlePolicy, nullptr);

     auto iceTransportPolicy = iceTransportPolicyFromConfiguration(configuration);
     g_object_set(m_webrtcBin.get(), "ice-transport-policy", iceTransportPolicy, nullptr);
